  "metadata": {
    "localmaxxing": {
      "backend": null,
      "batch_size": 1,
      "hardware_label": "RTX 3080",
      "notes": "131K context on a 10GB card via --n-cpu-moe 27 (experts of the first 27 of 41 layers on CPU). Five reps gave 27.2 / 50.9 / 64.4 / 64.4 / 64.9 tok/s -- a clear cold start then a stable plateau, so the median of 5 (64.4) is a fair warm figure here. IMPORTANT for anyone benchmarking CPU-offloaded MoE: the first one or two requests are dominated by cold expert page-in and understate steady-state badly; a 10-token prompt generating 200 tokens reports only ~8 tok/s for this model because it never leaves that regime. MTP was tested and is NOT worth enabling here: the draft head's own footprint pushes this config into host spill (882 MiB shared, decode down to 18 tok/s), and at an offload level with headroom it was within noise of no-MTP. Measured on an RTX 3080 10GB. Decode is the MEDIAN of 5 reps, not the best. Prompt is deliberately non-repetitive (repeated filler inflates decode on speculative setups by ~25%) and ignore_eos is set so output token count is identical across runs. Peak VRAM 9842 MiB with 370 MiB host-shared; elevated host-shared only indicates spill when the decode rate drops with it.",
      "observed_command": "llama-server \\\n  -m Ornith-1.5-35B-Q4_K_M.gguf \\\n  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8099 \\\n  --device CUDA0 --n-gpu-layers 99 \\\n  --ctx-size 131072 \\\n  --flash-attn on \\\n  --cache-type-k q8_0 --cache-type-v q8_0 \\\n  --parallel 1 --jinja \\\n  --spec-type none",
